      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In *Vaughan v. Maritime Logistics Ltd [2022]*, the High Court found Maritime Logistics Ltd liable for breaching its duty of care under the Merchant Shipping Act 1995 due to the failure to maintain traction sensors on cargo vessels. The judgment relied on *Donoghue v Stevenson [1932]* to establish the general principle of duty of care, applied the three-stage test from *Caparo Industries plc v Dickman [1990]* to determine the existence of duty, breach, and causation, and referenced *Robinson v Chief Constable of West Yorkshire Police [2018]* to illustrate the application of existing precedents to negligence duties. The court held that Maritime Logistics Ltd's negligence directly resulted in the incident, affirming the importance of adhering to established safety standards in maritime operations.",
